diff --git a/docs/ref/models/querysets.txt b/docs/ref/models/querysets.txt
index 223bb452b0..951783a161 100644
--- a/docs/ref/models/querysets.txt
+++ b/docs/ref/models/querysets.txt
@@ -1328,6 +1328,18 @@ where prefetching with a custom ``QuerySet`` is useful:
     >>> restaurants = Restaurant.objects.prefetch_related(
     ...     Prefetch('best_pizza', queryset=queryset))
 
+The ``queryset`` argument of ``Prefetch`` may be sliced. The slice is applied
+to the related objects of each instance, e.g. to prefetch the first three
+pizzas of every restaurant::
+
+    >>> restaurants = Restaurant.objects.prefetch_related(
+    ...     Prefetch('pizzas', queryset=Pizza.objects.order_by('name')[:3],
+    ...              to_attr='first_pizzas'))
+
+This requires a database that supports window functions; otherwise
+:exc:`~django.db.NotSupportedError` is raised. It is supported for reverse
+``ForeignKey``, ``ManyToManyField``, and ``GenericRelation`` lookups.
+
 When using multiple databases, ``Prefetch`` will respect your choice of
 database. If the inner query does not specify a database, it will use the
 database selected by the outer query. All of the following are valid::
